A||||6||BAM-BAM||How is Anthony Barber doing?||||12||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||01-28-2001||03:36 PM||||  So far, I have only heard that we are a little short on the Anthony Barber Fund, but I'm optimistic that that will change. What we haven't heard is, how is Anthony doing? Everytime I see that Photo of his car, I don't know weather he will thank the Fiero's construction for saving him or curse it as the cause of his injuries. I hope the first! Perhaps Wayne or Mike have some answers for us. Here's praying for the best!!<P>  Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-28-2001||03:59 PM||||I just got this e-mail from Chip (Anthony's friend):<P>Update on Anthony:<P>Anthony has been transferred to Craig Hostpital just outside of Denver.<BR>Craig specializes in brain/spine injuries.  I'm told that Christopher Reeves<BR>went there after his accident.  After some<BR>tests and evaluations they have found some things that they do need to work<BR>with him on, some difficulties with shapes/spatial relationships and things<BR>like that.  Otherwise, his memory is very much improved.  They are working<BR>with him on his leg a little as well-- he uses a wheelchair and a walker,<BR>but still does not put a lot of weight on it.<P>Craig is very different from St. Anthony's.  I visited Anthony on Monday,<BR>and his mood is so much better.  I would compare his room at Craig to a dorm<BR>room, more than a hospital room--It's even got a fridge...He's wearing<BR>regular clothes now, and is a little more 'up and about', so he's a little<BR>less bored.  Still don't know how long his stay will be, or how long his<BR>out-patient care will be.  I just wanted to let you guys know that Anthony<BR>continues to get better, and he and his family (as well as myself and my<BR>family) appreciate your continued prayers and support.<P>Chip<BR>||||reg||10
